WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.069
Living on the Moon needs light and machines that keep working.

2
00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:08.631
Reprise brings making and repair to the Moon.

3
00:00:08.631 --> 00:00:13.416
Outside, robots use the vacuum to coat reflective films.

4
00:00:13.416 --> 00:00:17.381
These surfaces direct sunlight towards the settlement.

5
00:00:17.381 --> 00:00:23.187
A covered street links three courts where robots clean, prepare and coat the films.

6
00:00:23.187 --> 00:00:27.139
Worn surfaces return along this street for renewal.

7
00:00:27.139 --> 00:00:31.830
Inside, beneath protective regolith, people take over.

8
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:36.910
They inspect components and repair the machinery that keeps the settlement working.

9
00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:43.550
Where resources are scarce, replacing worn film and reusing frames makes materials last.

10
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:48.980
Workbenches, shared tables and quiet spaces bring people together.

11
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:53.254
The workshop supports a lasting human presence on the Moon.

12
00:00:53.254 --> 00:00:56.092
Here, a community cares for what it builds.
